meta {
  name: Get Inventory In Storage
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/inventory/search/by_room_storage/:room/:storage
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  room: Main Room
  storage: Shelf
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Get Inventory In Storage
  
  This request is used to get all inventory data in layout page. This request interacts with the MySQL database, and has a protected routes.
  
  ## Path Parameters
  
  | Name    | Type   | Required | Description             | Example    |
  |---------|--------|----------|---------------------------|------------|
  | room    | string | yes      | Inventory storage's room | Main Room  |
  | storage | string | yes      | Inventory storage         | Main Table |
  
  ## Responses
  
  **200 — Inventory fetched successfully.** Ordered in descending order by `inventory_name`
  ```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "inventory fetched",
    "data": [
      {
        "id": "6f59235e-c398-8a83-2f95-3f1fbe95ca6e",
        "inventory_name": "Cake",
        "inventory_unit": "Pcs",
        "inventory_vol": 1,
        "inventory_price": 200000,
        "inventory_category": "Food And Beverages"
      }
    ]
  }
  ```
  
  **401 — protected route need to include sign in token as authorization bearer**
  ```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "you need to include the authorization token from login"
  }
  ```
  
  **404 — inventory failed to fetched**
  ```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "inventory not found"
  }
  ```
  
  **500 — Internal Server Error**
  ```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "something wrong. please contact admin"
  }
  ```
}
